finding: The claim that poseGltfScene's contract is unchanged fails for mutated animations. src/extras/gltf/kernel.ts:166-173 caches uploaded clips solely by GltfAnimation identity and never refreshes their channels or sampler arrays. Before the port, poseGltfScene called evaluateGltfAnimation on the supplied animation each time, so edits were observed. GltfAnimation's channels, samplers and Float32Array contents remain publicly mutable. The new loadGltfScene JSDoc (scene.ts:63-65) instead imposes an immutability requirement; that is a contract change, not an equivalent port. Independent no-tree-change probe using the shipped embedded kernel: one root node, LINEAR translation at times [0,1] with x values [0,2]. poseGltfScene at .5 returned x=1. Mutate that same sampler output's final x to 8, call poseGltfScene again at .5: x stays 1. evaluateGltfAnimation on the same node and animation returns x=4; passing a new animation identity to poseGltfScene also returns 4. Thus standalone evaluation and scene posing now disagree for the identical supplied clip. Existing records only evaluate unchanged clips and all pass despite this failure.
